@commentService = http://localhost:8081
@profanityService = http://localhost:8082
@contentType = application/json

### Create a clean comment (ProfanityService checks it and lets it through)
POST {{commentService}}/api/comments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "articleId": 1,
  "author": "John",
  "text": "Great article, thanks for sharing!"
}

### Create a comment containing a banned word - rejected with 400
POST {{commentService}}/api/comments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "articleId": 1,
  "author": "John",
  "text": "This article is written by an idiot."
}

### List every comment for an article
GET {{commentService}}/api/comments/article/1

### Read one comment back (replace 1 with the id returned above)
GET {{commentService}}/api/comments/1

### Delete it
DELETE {{commentService}}/api/comments/1

### --- Circuit breaker demo -------------------------------------------
### 1. Stop profanity-service: docker compose stop profanity-service
### 2. Post a few comments in a row - the first 3 each wait out the
###    3s HttpClient timeout before falling back; after 3 failures the
###    circuit opens and every comment after that is accepted instantly
###    with ProfanityChecked = false, because CommentService stops even
###    trying to reach ProfanityService for 30 seconds.
POST {{commentService}}/api/comments
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "articleId": 1,
  "author": "John",
  "text": "Comment posted while ProfanityService is down."
}
